/**
 * @page data_structures_reference Data Structures Reference
 * @brief A guided reference to ascii-chat's data structures.
 * @ingroup module_data_structures
 *
 * Start with the generated Data Structures index for the complete alphabetical
 * list. This page adds the design context that is easy to miss when browsing
 * declarations: which subsystem owns a type, what kind of state it carries,
 * and where to look for lifecycle and concurrency rules.
 */
/**
 * @struct options_t
 * @brief The immutable, RCU-published snapshot of every runtime option. It carries the selected mode, media and terminal settings, network and discovery endpoints, authentication and encryption policy, logging controls, and the explicit-value markers used when defaults are merged. Readers borrow the current snapshot through `options_get()`; writers create a replacement rather than mutating a snapshot in place.
 */
/**
 * @struct acds_create_key_set_t
   * @brief Stores `request`, `reserved string`, and `count`. The owning acds create key set code updates these members during setup, work, and cleanup; pointers remain owned by the subsystem that created them.
 */
/**
 * @struct acds_protocol_t
   * @brief Stores `send`, `user data`, `state`, `terminal`, `auto join`, `require webrtc`, `error`, and `join`. The owning acds protocol code updates these members during setup, work, and cleanup; pointers remain owned by the subsystem that created them.
 */
