/**
 * @struct crypto_context_t
 * @brief Owns one endpoint's cryptographic state: ephemeral and peer keys, the derived shared and password keys, negotiated nonce/MAC sizes, handshake and authentication nonces, encryption counters, session identity, and temporary keys used during rekeying. It is initialized and wiped by the crypto API; transports borrow the context to seal and open packets but do not copy or free its secret material.
 */
